	"claims": [
		{
			"id": "development-entrance",
			"statement": "The current generic development entrance preserves discovery/probe/feedback/warm behavior and never treats feedback or save as exact-root acceptance. It corrects original F1 by repeating trial-source and destination checks after the potentially slow real runtime/import queries, immediately before the existing atomic compare-and-write. Current deterministic and actual Lean regression changes a dependency source while leaving old imported artifacts unchanged and requires stale rejection without materializing the target; concurrent destination edits are also retained. This is observed freshness, not an OS-wide transaction.",
			"verification": "software"
		},
		{
			"id": "strict-and-continuation",
			"statement": "The nonempty independently authored target list still delegates roots to the retained verifier. Its digest now binds the bytes actually parsed. Original F2 is corrected by a terminal recheck of every selected manifest with common source/configuration, declared non-Lean input, target-list, runtime/tool and listed-evidence bindings observed before and after that complete pass; row and summary flags are recomputed from terminal results and the common binding, and manifest identity remains bound. Current actual Lean regressions reject both a first-root mutation before second-root compilation and a mutation immediately after both real terminal checks returned true. Durable status uses the same common-observation boundary; completion alone is not proof. This does not claim an OS-wide filesystem transaction.",
			"verification": "software"
		},
		{
			"id": "native-review-identity",
			"statement": "The unchanged review adapter retains legacy UUIDs and true collaboration.spawn_agent canonical task identities with explicit fork_turns none, exact frozen prompt, matching task suffix and author exclusion. Only matching FINAL_ANSWER/full report completes it; missing or ordinary messages remain incomplete. The supplied original actual dispatch/completion/CHANGES_REQUIRED receipt demonstrates current protocol use without inventing UUIDs. Its trust boundary is coordinator-attested transcripts, not service authentication, and original approval of this unchanged claim does not approve the correction as a whole.",
			"verification": "software"
		},
		{
			"id": "hidden-windows-processes",
			"statement": "The unchanged native Windows Lean/Lake, LSP, rg and workflow child paths retain CREATE_NO_WINDOW behavior and original POSIX process setup. Current native portable and workflow reruns pass, including zero GetConsoleWindow. No Linux/WSL live run or universal UI no-flicker claim is made.",
			"verification": "software"
		}
	],
